## 5. Non-Commercial Restriction

**5.1 Definition of "Commercial Use."** "Commercial Use" means any use, reproduction, Distribution, hosting, deployment, or other exploitation of the Software or any Derivative Work, in whole or in material part, that is intended for or directed toward commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or private financial gain, whether the gain is realized directly or indirectly. Without limiting the foregoing, Commercial Use includes, by way of illustration and not limitation:

(a) selling, licensing, leasing, or renting the Software or any Derivative Work, in Source Form or Compiled Form, whether modified or unmodified, and whether alone or as part of a larger work;

(b) charging any fee, price, or other monetary consideration for access to, download of, distribution of, or use of the Software or any Compiled Form thereof, including nominal, "at-cost," or "convenience" fees;

(c) incorporating the Software, in whole or in part, into any product, application, plugin, template, or service that is sold, licensed for a fee, or offered as part of a paid bundle, including bundling the Software with paid software, paid hardware, or a paid installer;

(d) offering the Software or a Derivative Work as a hosted, cloud-based, or Software-as-a-Service ("SaaS") offering for which end users pay a fee, subscription, or other consideration, or from which the operator otherwise derives revenue in connection with the offering;

(e) using the Software to deliver paid consulting, integration, support, maintenance, hosting, or training services where the Software constitutes the primary subject matter or primary source of value of the service offered ("support-washing");

(f) Distributing the Software or a Derivative Work through any channel that generates advertising revenue, referral revenue, affiliate revenue, sponsorship revenue, or other indirect monetary benefit attributable to that Distribution;

(g) gating, unlocking, or offering enhanced features, functionality, priority access, or removal of limitations in exchange for donations, tips, pledges, subscriptions, or similar consideration tied to the Software;

(h) reselling, re-licensing, or otherwise transferring for consideration a Fork, Derivative Work, or Compiled Form of the Software;

(i) any use by, or on behalf of, a for-profit entity in connection with the generation of revenue, the reduction of costs passed on to paying customers, or the creation of a competitive commercial advantage, where the Software forms a material part of the commercial product, service, or infrastructure involved; and

(j) any other direct or indirect method of monetization of the Software, however structured or labeled, that is designed or reasonably likely to circumvent the intent of this Section 5.

**5.2 Restriction.** Except as expressly authorized in a separate written commercial license agreement executed by the Copyright Holder, You may NOT engage in Commercial Use of the Software or any Derivative Work, in whole or in part, in original or modified form. This restriction:

(a) applies regardless of the license or terms You choose to apply to Your own original Contributions within a Derivative Work; and

(b) applies to any Fork, Derivative Work, or Compiled Form to the extent that it incorporates, is derived from, depends upon, or could not reasonably exist or function without the Software.

**5.3 Non-Commercial Use — Illustrative Safe Harbor.** For the avoidance of doubt, and without limiting the generality of Section 1.11, the following do not, by themselves, constitute Commercial Use:

(a) hosting a free, publicly accessible copy, mirror, or Fork of the Software's Source Form on a platform such as GitHub or GitLab, provided no fee, subscription, or other consideration is charged for access to it;

(b) forking, studying, modifying, or contributing to the Software as part of open-source collaboration, where no Contributor receives monetary compensation for the Software itself;

(c) accepting unconditional, voluntary donations that do not unlock any feature, functionality, priority access, or other material benefit tied to the Software;

(d) use of the Software for personal projects, hobbyist projects, academic coursework, classroom instruction, or non-commercial scholarly research and publication; and

(e) internal, non-production evaluation, testing, or research use of the Software by an employee or contractor of a commercial entity, provided that the Software is not thereby incorporated into, or made a component of, any product or service offered to third parties.

**5.4 Requesting Commercial Permission.** A party wishing to make Commercial Use of the Software must first obtain the prior written permission of the Copyright Holder, which may take the form of a separate commercial license agreement and may be subject to fees or other terms at the Copyright Holder's sole discretion. Requests may be directed to: **contact@qhuyy.tech**. Nothing in this License obligates the Copyright Holder to grant such permission on any particular terms, or at all.

